exports[`snapshots of the layout IR as text about-this-vault.md @ 80 1`] = `
"▌ About this vault

slipbox's demo vault, and the material its tests render. Everything in it is
invented: the Halden Ridge Observatory, its town, its people and its instruments
do not exist. Open it with bun src/main.ts examples/vault, or start at home.

The notes read like a real team's working notes on purpose. Real notes contain
awkward things — tables too wide for any screen, unbreakable paths, lines over
the length limit, a malformed heading — and a renderer is only as good as its
worst input. So these notes keep those things, and some deliberately break the
house style that writing-guide describes.

▌ What each note is for

┌────────────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Note                               │ Exercises                               │
╞════════════════════════════════════╪═════════════════════════════════════════╡
│ equipment/telescope-comparison.md  │ the table allocator's hardest case:     │
│                                    │ seven columns, cells of 250 characters  │
├────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ equipment/instrument-inventory.md  │ table rows of 500+ characters to wrap,  │
│                                    │ never overflow; emoji in cells          │
├────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ logs/observing-log-2026.md         │ throughput: 30 tables and 216 rows in   │
│                                    │ one note                                │
├────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ scratch/wrap-probe.md              │ a small wide-table case with            │
│                                    │ unbreakable tokens, for fast iteration  │
├────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ handbook/writing-guide.md          │ YAML frontmatter, tables and fences:    │
│                                    │ the common mixture                      │
├────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ software/pipeline-cookbook.md      │ fences in a dozen languages, mermaid,   │
│                                    │ $$ math, ~~~, indented code, tabs       │
├────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ handbook/operations-handbook.md    │ 1,200+ lines, h1–h6, setext, callouts,  │
│                                    │ a 4-deep checklist, a long heading      │
├────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ handbook/writing-guide.md (HTML)   │ inline HTML, a comment, <details>;      │
│                                    │ lists from 0), 7., 998.                 │
├────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ equipment/instrument-inventory.md  │ broken images: missing files, empty alt │
│ (photos)                           │ text                                    │
├────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ meetings/2026-09-14-weekly.md      │ hard breaks (two spaces, backslash) and │
│                                    │ a struck-out decision                   │
├────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ people/kenji-mori.md               │ frontmatter with a nested map, a block  │
│                                    │ string and a long key                   │
├────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ scratch/broken-frontmatter.md      │ frontmatter that is not valid YAML      │
├────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ projects/variable-star-survey.md   │ long prose with code, tables, quotes    │
│                                    │ and a block id: the ordinary case       │
├────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ projects/dome-refit.md             │ TOML frontmatter, every callout kind    │
│                                    │ (GitHub's capitals, nested), numbered   │
│                                    │ tasks                                   │
├────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ projects/dome-refit.md (again)     │ * and + bullets, a www. autolink, an    │
│                                    │ image that exists (attachments/)        │
├────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ projects/*.md (tags)               │ #tags in the text beside frontmatter    │
│                                    │ tags, nested ones (#dome/shutter):      │
│                                    │ space f t                               │
├────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ people/partners-and-names.md       │ every link form, broken links,          │
│                                    │ footnotes; CJK, emoji, ZWJ, RTL widths  │
├────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ home.md, people/, meetings/        │ a linked graph: backlinks, tasks,       │
│                                    │ heading references, two notes of one    │
│                                    │ name                                    │
├────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ logs/observing-log-2026.md (again) │ repeated ### Weather headings, an       │
│                                    │ in-note #anchor link                    │
├────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ software/halley/halley.toml        │ a data file: sections, comments,        │
│                                    │ [[telescope]] records, path links       │
├────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ software/halley/targets.yaml,      │ YAML records as a table, nested maps;   │
│ .schema.json                       │ JSON with $schema, $ref                 │
├────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ software/nightjar/openapi.json     │ deep JSON as a tree: $ref pointers      │
│                                    │ followed, records in the tree           │
├────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ software/nightjar/deploy.yaml      │ a YAML tree: uneven lists of objects,   │
│                                    │ anchors and aliases, a block string     │
├────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ software/nightjar/environments.    │ several YAML documents (---); a flat    │
│ yaml, package.json                 │ manifest                                │
├────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ software/halley/logging.ini,       │ INI: ;, # comments, a comment after a   │
│ archive.properties                 │ value; dotted keys                      │
├────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ equipment/mount-aster.cfg,         │ .cfg with dotted sections; .env with    │
│ nightjar/nightjar.env              │ export, quotes                          │
├────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ equipment/eyepieces.tsv            │ TSV: tabs, a quoted field, cells that   │
│                                    │ wrap                                    │
├────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ logs/photometry-2026.csv           │ 2,600 rows: past the 2,000-row render   │
│                                    │ cap, quoted fields, empty cells         │
├────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ equipment/filters.csv              │ CSV: quoted fields with commas and "",  │
│                                    │ empty cells                             │
├────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ software/halley/reduce.py,         │ tree-sitter: docstrings, heredocs, an   │
│ night.sh                           │ outline, links in comments              │
├────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ nightjar/src/server.ts,            │ TypeScript, JavaScript: enums,          │
│ public/app.js                      │ interfaces, classes, template strings   │
├────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ uploader/main.go,                  │ Go and Rust: types, methods, traits,    │
│ stacker/src/main.rs                │ impl, raw strings, doc comments         │
├────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ software/halley/dome.lua           │ Lua: local function, function t.m, long │
│                                    │ strings and comments                    │
├────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ scratch/half-written.py,           │ a syntax error in code; a data file     │
│ broken-config.json                 │ that doesn't parse                      │
├────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ logs/dome-log.org,                 │ formats slipbox doesn't read as notes:  │
│ handbook/safety-card.adoc          │ text files, source mode                 │
├────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ outreach/, outreach/school-visits/ │ vaults nested in this one: links across │
│                                    │ vaults, by path (below)                 │
└────────────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────────┘

▌ Nested vaults

This vault is named halden (.slipbox/config.toml, [vault]), and holds two more,
each with a .slipbox/ of its own — boundaries, not folders of this one:

• outreach/, the vault outreach (alias public): the public programme;
• outreach/school-visits/, the vault outreach-school-visits, nested in that.

Their notes link across all three by path, as every link is (slipbox's links are
plain paths): into a nested vault ([…](school-visits/index.md)), out of one
(../handbook/operations-handbook.md, ../../handbook/safety-card.adoc), with a
heading (#o2-night-assistant-owns-the-night-2025-02), and to a folder this
machine doesn't have (../../archive/2019-season.md). To try them: open this
vault, and

• the explorer shows outreach with a vault's icon; enter goes into it;
• the outreach link at the end of home goes there too, and ctrl+o comes back;
• space l b on home.md lists the backlinks from outreach and school-visits;
• space v v lists the vaults; space n m renames a note and fixes the links in
  all three.

scripts/sample-metrics.ts measures what each note exercises (lines, longest
line, tables and rows, fences and their languages, headings, links, wide and
right-to-left characters), so a change to a note can be checked against what it
has to keep covering.

▌ What isn't here

The vault cases — name collisions, CRLF, a BOM, Latin-1, no final newline, a
hostile note full of terminal escapes, symlinks, ignored folders, a nested vault
— live in the test fixture vault, tests/fixtures/vault/, since they don't belong
in a demo. Still missing anywhere:

• A pathological file. No multi-megabyte note, and no .md file that is really a
  log.
• Mermaid and LaTeX, rendered. software/pipeline-cookbook.md now has a mermaid
  fence and a $$ block, but slipbox shows both as code; drawing them is a
  deferred feature.

Some links are unresolved on purpose, so the link index always has failures to
report:

• people/partners-and-names.md: visiting-rota.md (a note nobody has written
  yet), dome-diagram.png and <../scratch/wrap probe copy.md>; and
  ../home.md#no-such-heading and ../projects/variable-star-survey.md#^nope,
  whose notes exist but whose heading and block don't.
• handbook/writing-guide.md: ../projects/dunmore-refurbishment.md,
  ../incidents/2026-03-14-fw8-stuck.md, ../reports/template.md and glossary.md
  (twice).
• equipment/instrument-inventory.md: images/lyra-slit.png, images/tern-frame.jpg
  and missing-flat-field.png, placeholders for photos not yet taken.
• outreach/index.md: ../../archive/2019-season.md, in a folder no machine has."
`;

