▎ Visitors will point white phone torches at the terrace. Smile, hand them a red
▎ one, repeat.

▌ O25: Documentation categories

Decision: Observatory documentation falls into four categories, each with a
home: this handbook (decisions and standing procedures), runbooks (step-by-step
for one task), logs (what happened), and ideas (what might happen one day). Why:
The workshop wiki had become a single page titled "Stuff", 14,000 words long,
with the dome motor wiring diagram between a cake rota and a list of meteor
showers.

▌ What goes where

┌──────────┬──────────────┬───────────────────────┬────────────────────────────┐
│ Category │ Home         │ Changes when          │ Example                    │
╞══════════╪══════════════╪═══════════════════════╪════════════════════════════╡
│ Handbook │ this file    │ a decision is made or │ O6 weather limits          │
│          │              │ reversed              │                            │
├──────────┼──────────────┼───────────────────────┼────────────────────────────┤
│ Runbooks │ runbooks/    │ the procedure changes │ Replacing the dome shutter │
│          │              │                       │ belt                       │
├──────────┼──────────────┼───────────────────────┼────────────────────────────┤
│ Logs     │ logs/ and    │ every night, every    │ 2025-05-14 night log       │
│          │ night logs   │ maintenance visit     │                            │
├──────────┼──────────────┼───────────────────────┼────────────────────────────┤
│ Ideas    │ ideas/       │ whenever someone has  │ A second all-sky camera on │
│          │              │ one                   │ the roll-off               │
└──────────┴──────────────┴───────────────────────┴────────────────────────────┘

▌ Why ideas are separate from runbooks

An idea that sits in the runbooks folder looks like a procedure. In March 2025 a
volunteer found an "idea" note describing how one might realign Brill's finder
and followed it, step by step, on a night when nobody had checked whether the
idea worked. It did not. Ideas now live in their own folder with a banner at the
top of each: "Not a procedure. Do not follow."

▌ Why the handbook links out rather than inlining runbooks

A handbook entry says what we decided and why. A runbook says how. When the how
changes (a new belt supplier, a different torque value), the decision usually
does not. Keeping them apart means changing a torque value does not rewrite
history.

▌ Naming

• Handbook entries: O<number>: <short title>, the number never reused.
• Runbooks: verb first, replace-shutter-belt.md, realign-brill-finder.md.
• Logs: date first, 2025-05-14-night.md, 2025-06-02-dunmore-bench.md.
• Ideas: noun first, second-allsky-camera.md.

▌ O26: Meteor Watch detections are auto-filed, human-confirmed (2025-08)

Decision: The Tern all-sky camera's detection software files candidate meteors
automatically into stacks, but nothing is published until a human confirms it.
Why: In its first week Tern "detected" 212 meteors, 190 of which were aircraft,
14 were a moth, and 8 were meteors. The moth has since been named Gerald.

┌─────────────────────┬────────────┬─────────────────────┬─────────────────────┐
│ Candidate type      │ Auto-filed │ Human review needed │ Publishable         │
╞═════════════════════╪════════════╪═════════════════════╪═════════════════════╡
│ Single-frame streak │ yes        │ yes                 │ after review        │
├─────────────────────┼────────────┼─────────────────────┼─────────────────────┤
│ Multi-frame track   │ yes        │ yes                 │ after review        │
├─────────────────────┼────────────┼─────────────────────┼─────────────────────┤
│ Blinking track      │ no         │ n/a                 │ never (aircraft)    │
├─────────────────────┼────────────┼─────────────────────┼─────────────────────┤
│ Slow blob           │ no         │ n/a                 │ never (insect,      │
│                     │            │                     │ cloud, Gerald)      │
└─────────────────────┴────────────┴─────────────────────┴─────────────────────┘

▌ O27: Dark Sky Campaign data is shared openly (2025-09)

Decision: Sky brightness readings taken for the Dark Sky Campaign are published
as open data every month, raw and uncorrected, alongside a plain-language
summary for the Marrowby council. Why: The council asked for "the numbers, not
your interpretation". Fair.

The summary follows a fixed template so month-to-month comparisons are easy. See
the campaign page <https://example.org/dark-sky/marrowby> for the published
months.

▎ Ada, at the September meeting: "If the numbers go the wrong way, we publish
▎ those too. Especially those."

