▌ O34: Visiting astronomers get a buddy (2025-11)

Decision: Every visiting astronomer is paired with a staff buddy for the length
of their visit. Why: Kenji Mori's first visit from the Kiso-Hara Astronomical
Society went fine, but he spent his first evening looking for the kettle, the
fuse box and, eventually, anyone.

The buddy:

• Meets the visitor at the Marrowby bus stop or the car park.
• Walks them through O4, O5 and O8 in person.
• Shows them the kettle.
• Checks in daily, and at least once during their first night.

▌ O35: Intern projects are real projects (2025-12)

Decision: Student interns work on something the observatory actually needs, with
a named mentor, a written goal, and a presentation at the end. Why: Min-jun
Seo's placement produced the Tern false-positive filter that now keeps Gerald
out of the meteor catalogue. Make-work produces nothing.

