▌ O36: Dome shutter maintenance (2025-12)

Decision: The dome shutter belt, rollers and limit switches are inspected
monthly and the belt replaced every two years or at the first sign of fraying,
whichever comes first. Why: The belt is the one part whose failure leaves the
dome open in the rain.

▌ Monthly inspection

• Visually inspect the belt along its full length with the slit at 50 %.
• Check roller bearings for play by hand, power isolated.
• Trigger each limit switch manually and confirm the controller sees it.
• Wipe the rain sensor with a dry cloth.
• Log the inspection with initials and any findings.

The same inspection as the tick sheet in the binder, which nests because the
shutter does:

☐ Shutter
  ☐ Belt
    ☑ Upper run, slit at 50 %
    ☐ Lower run, slit closed
      ☐ Splice plate bolts, all six
      ☐ Tension gauge reads 40–45 N
  ☐ Limit switches
    ☐ Open limit
    ☐ Closed limit
☐ Rain sensor wiped

▌ Belt replacement

The belt replacement runbook lives at runbooks/replace-shutter-belt.md. It takes
two people and most of a day. Book it for a cloudy forecast, which on the ridge
is not hard.

▌ Manual close

If the shutter motor fails with the slit open, the slit can be wound closed by
hand with the crank stored behind the control room door. It takes about 140
turns. Two people take turns. Bring the crank back.

▎ Every night assistant winds the slit closed by hand once during training, on a
▎ dry afternoon, so the first time they do it is not at 03:00 in sleet.

▌ Winding by hand, in detail

Isolate the shutter motor at the red switch first; the crank will fight a live
motor and win. Engage the crank on the hex boss below the drive pulley and turn
clockwise, looking up.

▌ If the crank slips

The crank's pin shears before the gearbox does, by design. Spare pins are in the
tin taped inside the control room door.

▌ Replacing the shear pin

Knock the stub out with the 4 mm drift, fit a new pin, and log the replacement:
a slipping crank usually means the belt is binding, and that is a fault for
Tomasz, not a pin for the tin.

▌ O37: Power cuts and the UPS (2026-01)

Decision: On mains failure the UPS carries ridge-ctl, the dome controller and
the mount for at least 20 minutes, long enough to park and close. Everything
else drops. Why: The ridge loses mains about six times a year, usually in winter
storms, which are also the nights you most want the dome shut.

┌─────────────────────────┬─────┬─────────────┬────────────────────────────────┐
│ Load                    │ On  │ Runtime at  │ Notes                          │
│                         │ UPS │ full load   │                                │
╞═════════════════════════╪═════╪═════════════╪════════════════════════════════╡
│ ridge-ctl               │ yes │ 45 min      │                                │
├─────────────────────────┼─────┼─────────────┼────────────────────────────────┤
│ Dome controller + motor │ yes │ 25 min      │ Motor draw dominates           │
├─────────────────────────┼─────┼─────────────┼────────────────────────────────┤
│ Aster mount             │ yes │ 40 min      │                                │
├─────────────────────────┼─────┼─────────────┼────────────────────────────────┤
│ HCAM-2 + chiller        │ no  │ n/a         │ Warms up slowly; no harm done  │
├─────────────────────────┼─────┼─────────────┼────────────────────────────────┤
│ ridge-arch              │ own │ 60 min      │ Shuts down cleanly after 10    │
│                         │ UPS │             │ min on battery                 │
├─────────────────────────┼─────┼─────────────┼────────────────────────────────┤
│ ridge-web               │ no  │ n/a         │ The public site can wait       │
├─────────────────────────┼─────┼─────────────┼────────────────────────────────┤
│ Pavilion lights         │ no  │ n/a         │ Emergency lighting has its own │
│                         │     │             │ batteries                      │
└─────────────────────────┴─────┴─────────────┴────────────────────────────────┘

On a power cut during an observing night:

1. nightjar notices the UPS signal and aborts the current exposure.
2. The mount parks automatically.
3. The night assistant closes the slit from the controller, or by hand (O36) if
   the controller is not responding.
4. The night assistant logs a fault line and goes home if power is not back in
   an hour.

▌ O38: Snow on the dome (2026-01)

Decision: The dome does not open with snow on it, even if the sky is clear. Why:
Snow sliding off an opening shutter falls into the dome, onto the telescope,
which is the one place it must never be.

Clearing snow is a daytime job, from the ground, with the long brush. Never from
the catwalk (O8 applies twice as hard in winter).

▌ O39: Quill seeing values in FITS headers (2026-01)

Decision: Every HCAM-2 frame records the most recent Quill FWHM value and its
age in the FITS header. Why: Reducers kept asking "what was the seeing?" and the
answer was always in a different log.

                                                                           text
 QUILLFWH=                 1.84 / Quill seeing FWHM, arcsec, zenith-corrected
 QUILLAGE=                   42 / seconds since the Quill measurement above was
↪ taken, at frame start
 QUILLVER= 'q2.3.1'             / Quill firmware


▌ O40: The halley configuration file (2026-02)

Decision: halley reads one configuration file per season, checked into
ridge-ops, with comments on every non-obvious value. Why: A value without a
reason gets "tidied" by the next person.

                                                                           toml
 # /etc/halley/season-2025-26.toml — pinned for the 2025–26 season (O18)
 [photometry]
 aperture_radius_fwhm = 1.5     # multiples of the frame's measured FWHM
 annulus_inner_fwhm   = 3.0
 annulus_outer_fwhm   = 5.0
 zero_point_source    = "calibration-stars"   # see O15; never the catalogue ze
↪ro point, which is off by 0.02 in B for our filter set

 [flat]
 prefer    = "twilight"
 fallback  = "dome"       # see O17 for why dome flats are a last resort
 max_age_d = 7

 [archive]
 root     = "/archive"
 database = "postgresql://halley@ridge-arch/stacks"


▌ O41: Incident reviews are blameless and written down (2026-02)

Decision: Every incident that damages equipment, loses data, or makes someone
feel unsafe gets a written review within a week, in the format below. Why:
People who are blamed stop reporting. We would like the reports.

▌ Review format

• What happened, in time order, UTC.
• What we expected to happen instead.
• Why the difference, as far as we can tell.
• What we are changing, each with an owner and a date.
• What we are deliberately not changing, and why.

