▌ O42: Red light only after dark (2026-02)

Decision: After astronomical dusk, only red light is used in the domes, the
roll-off, and on the terrace, including phone screens (night mode, lowest
brightness). Why: Dark adaptation takes twenty minutes to build and one phone
screen to destroy, and a white torch on the terrace spoils sixty people's view
at once.

Exceptions, in full:

• An injury or emergency: use any light you need, immediately.
• The workshop, with its door shut.
• The server room.

▎ Yusuf's note on the pavilion door, translated for the handbook: "Your eyes are
▎ the best instrument we own tonight. Please be gentle with them." 🔭

▌ O43: Volunteer observers (2026-03)

Decision: Volunteers may observe with Brill and Corvid unaccompanied after
training, and with Aster only with a night assistant present. Why: Yusuf Haddad
has logged more Brill hours than anyone on staff and deserves the keys to the
roll-off. Aster costs more than the pavilion.

