▌ O62: This handbook's own conventions (2026-09)

Decision: Entries follow the same shape so they can be skimmed in the control
room binder at 03:00.

• The heading is ## O<number>: <short title> (<YYYY-MM>).
• The first paragraph is Decision, then Why.
• Consequences appear when there are any worth writing down.
• Procedures longer than about ten steps move to a runbook (O25) and are linked,
  not inlined.
• A superseded entry keeps its text and gets a quoted note at the top pointing
  to its successor.
• Tables beat prose for anything with more than three comparable items.
• UTC throughout (O3).

▎ The handbook is a working document. If something here is wrong, the fix is a
▎ new entry or an edited one, not a sticky note on the binder. Sticky notes fall
▎ off, usually onto the floor of the Main Dome, where they are found in spring
▎ by whoever cleans it.

▌ O63: Open nights on the second Saturday (2025-03) — superseded by O24

▎ Superseded by O24 (2025-08). Open nights moved to the first and third Friday.
▎ The reasoning below is kept because the question of Saturdays keeps coming
▎ back (see O61).

Decision: One open night a month, on the second Saturday. Why: It was the night
the previous outreach coordinator was free.

Consequences: Attendance averaged 22, mostly couples. Families stayed away
because of Saturday sports. Lena's first survey (O24) came out of this.

▌ O64: Winter shutdown week (2026-09)

Decision: The observatory closes to visitors for the last week of December and
the first week of January. Science observing continues if a night assistant
volunteers. Why: Staff have families, the road up the ridge is often closed by
snow anyway, and the dome maintenance backlog (O36, O38) is easiest to clear
when nobody is booked.

During the shutdown:

• The pavilion heating is set to frost protection only.
• ridge-web shows a shutdown notice on the events calendar.
• The weekly offsite backup (O20) still runs; someone drives the disk down to
  Marrowby.
• The night assistant rota for the shutdown is agreed at the first Monday
  meeting in December.
• Anyone who does observe during the shutdown gets first pick of the leftover
  biscuits.

▌ O65: Tern camera housing heater (2026-09)

Decision: The Tern all-sky camera's dome heater runs whenever the dew margin is
below 4 °C, controlled by ridge-ctl from the Sable readings. Why: A dewed-up
all-sky dome reports 100 % cloud on a perfectly clear night, and the night
assistant, obeying O6, keeps the dome shut. This happened on three consecutive
clear nights in October 2025 before anyone climbed up to look.

                                                                             sh
 # /etc/cron.d/tern-heater — every two minutes, switch the Tern heater from the
↪ Sable dew margin.
 */2 * * * * ridge  /opt/ridge-ops/bin/tern-heater --on-below 4.0 --off-above 5
↪.0 --sable http://sable.example.invalid/api/v1/current --log /var/log/tern-hea
↪ter.log


Consequences: The heater draws 12 W and is not on the UPS (O37). A power cut
during a damp night means the all-sky frames go grey within twenty minutes; the
night assistant should treat Tern as blind until the heater has been back on for
half an hour.

▌ O66: Handbook entry template

Decision: New entries start from this template, copied into the end of the file.
Why: O62 describes the shape; a template makes it the default.

                                                                           text
 ## O<next number>: <short title> (<YYYY-MM>)

 **Decision:** <one or two sentences: what we do now>
 **Why:** <what happened, or what we expect to happen, that makes this the righ
↪t call>

 **Consequences:** <optional: what changes elsewhere, what we gave up, what to
↪watch for>


Before adding an entry, check:

• Is this a decision, or a procedure? Procedures go in runbooks/ (O25).
• Does it reverse an earlier entry? If so, mark that entry superseded in the
  same change.
• Has it been discussed at a Monday meeting (O56)? If not, bring it to the next
  one first.
• Will the person reading the binder at 03:00 understand it without asking
  anyone?

▎ Last word, from the first page of the original binder, in Tomasz's
▎ handwriting: "Write it down. The ridge forgets nothing, but people do."

▌ Appendix: shutter firmware

The dome controller runs vendor firmware that we patch ourselves, because the
vendor stopped shipping updates in 2024. Build names are long and are copied
exactly, never abbreviated.

▌ HRO-DOME-SHUTTER-FIRMWARE-3.2.1-rc4-patched-2026-03-14-build-00000000000042
  and why we still run it

It is the last build that honours the rain sensor while the slit is mid-travel.
Later builds finish the move first, which on a squally night means another
eleven seconds of open slit. Keep the image on the offsite disk next to the
ridge-ctl image (O45).

